 "purpose": "The data model of a fully analysed Dutch sentence (words with their word class, and the sentence parts) plus the bracket notation to write and check one.",
 "details": "Every sentence is fully analysed: each word belongs to a sentence part (zinsdeel) except punctuation, and the finite verb (pv) also belongs to the predicate (gezegde, wwg or nwg), as at school. The school year decides which parts are asked; the rest stays grey in the exercise. A sentence is written with brackets: '[o De juf] [pv geeft] [lv een boek].' (word class optional with '/vnw'; the predicate may be in pieces). A sentence with more than one pv (compound, 0.25.1) marks only the pv's and their subject, with '|' between the clauses. lees_haakjes parses the notation and raises ZinFout with a plain-language message; controleer validates an analysis; Zin.haakjes writes it back. No curses.",
 "module_docstring": "Een zin met zijn ontleding: de woorden (met hun woordsoort) en de zinsdelen (alleen data, geen curses).",
